{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And it shall be if they do not believe even these two signs.</b> For they will say: did not HaShem promise Abraham, saying, ״וְגַם אֶת הַגּוֹי אֲשֶׁר יַעֲבֹדוּ דָּן אָנֹכִי״ (Genesis 15:14)? And what is the sign that He will judge the nations full of corpses? Concerning this He said, ״וְלָקַחְתָּ מִמֵּימֵי הַיְאֹר וְשָׁפַכְתָּ הַיַּבָּשָׁה וְגוֹ׳ וְהָיוּ לְדָם בַּיַּבָּשֶׁת״. And it is known that the plague of the river is the plague of the god of Egypt, for they all believed in it, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 89:4), ״The wicked endure by their god, as it is said, ׳וְהִנֵּה עֹמֵד עַל הַיְאֹר׳״ etc. And all Egypt suffers when the river suffers, for all their success depends on the river. And the plague of the river is a great sign that HaShem will send upon them wrath and fury and trouble, upon them and upon their gods. And so the first plague was on the river, and this was the beginning of their downfall, through the turning of the river to blood. And likewise the last plague was at the waters of the Sea of Reeds. And after they see all these signs, they will be assured that ״מֵאַשְׁפֹּת יָרִים אֶבְיוֹן״ (Psalms 113:7) — through the nullification of cause and caused, and through the fulfillment of the promise ״וְגַם אֶת הַגּוֹי אֲשֶׁר יַעֲבֹדוּ דָּן אָנֹכִי״."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:22.415379250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}